wing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robob27/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robob27/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robob27/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robob27/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robob27/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robob27/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robob27/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robob27/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-13T09:15:29Z","updated_at":"2025-10-13T09:15:29Z","body":"The last commit should fix the scroll issue by ensuring that the `scroll_visible` member stays in sync with vscroll visibility when it gets updated due to `scroll_follow_visible_characters`. This makes us not spam set visibility on vscroll, preventing `drag.active` from getting set to `false` [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/scene/gui/scroll_bar.cpp#L423-L428).\r\n\r\nIt also moves the `_prepare_scroll_anchor` call that was previously inside the `scroll_follow_visible_characters` check into `NOTIFICATION_READY` - this seems to still fix the thick scrollbar issue without having to call `prepare_scroll_anchor` a bunch in draw.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3396573398/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3450696103","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111552#issuecomment-3450696103","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111552","id":3450696103,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7NrXGn","user":{"login":"robob27","id":2104555,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDQ1NTU="